Recompile the decompiled test classes for a release javac still supports.

ClassFileToJavaSourceTest recompiles what it decompiled, asking for the
Java release the class files came from. javac 12 dropped -source 6 and
javac 20 dropped 7, so on a current JDK 41 tests fail before compiling
anything; the harness already raised anything older than 6 for the same
reason, and now raises to the oldest release the running javac takes.

It also compiles with --release rather than -source/-target, against that
release's class library. Against JDK 21's, the decompiled
commons-collections4 4.1 clashes with SequencedCollection (addFirst,
addLast, firstEntry, lastEntry) whatever the decompiler does.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments

